+
+An ordinary leaf helper may interpret an entry buffer through a different pointee
+type. For device/constant pointers rooted in the same descriptor parameter, typed
+inlining selects one shared raw byte layout for the caller root and helper proxy;
+each cloned load/store retains its source type and the argument retains its offset.
+This also keeps entry accessibility facts available to coordinate placement across
+linked helper expansion. Conflicting local/workgroup allocations and pointers with
+no single descriptor root retain their typed call boundary. No new reflection or
+source-proof fields are needed, but translation/cache identities must change.
